Copyright (c) 2026 Forge Everything Team (Rexilyent and Team)

This is a source-available license, not an open-source one. You can read the
code, change it for yourself and help improve it, but you cannot share or
re-upload the mod or versions of it. After Rexilyent's death the mod becomes
free for anyone to change and share, as long as the pride flags stay in (see
section 6). The full terms are below.

1. Definitions

"The Mod" means Everything RGB Profiles: its source code, compiled builds,
default profile files, images, documentation and every other file in this
repository or in a release of it, except the Third-Party Components listed in
section 7.

"Official Sources" means the Mod's own project pages on Modrinth and
CurseForge, and the releases page of its GitHub repository.

2. What you may do

a. Download the Mod from an Official Source and use it, including in videos,
   streams and screenshots, whether or not those are monetised.

b. Include the Mod in a modpack published anywhere, as long as the modpack
   does not contain or re-host the Mod's files and instead has them downloaded
   from an Official Source when the pack is installed. For example:
   - a modpack on Modrinth or CurseForge that uses the Mod's project page on
     that platform;
   - a packwiz (or similar) modpack, hosted on GitHub or anywhere else, whose
     entry for the Mod points to a download on an Official Source.
   Committing, bundling or mirroring the Mod's jar inside the modpack itself,
   or in the modpack's repository, counts as redistribution under section 3a.

c. Read and study the source code, change it, and build changed versions for
   your own personal use.

d. Fork the repository on GitHub in order to contribute changes back to the
   Mod through pull requests.

3. What you may not do without written permission from the copyright holders

a. Redistribute the Mod, in compiled or source form, changed or unchanged,
   except as section 2 allows. This includes uploading it to any website,
   launcher or file host other than the Official Sources.

b. Publish, share or distribute a changed version of the Mod, or any other
   work that copies a substantial part of its source code or files.

c. Sell the Mod, charge for access to it, or put it behind a paywall.

d. Present the Mod, or any part of it, as your own work, or misrepresent
   where it came from.

4. Contributions

If you submit a contribution to the Mod (for example, a pull request), you
confirm that you have the right to submit it, and you grant the copyright
holders a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free and irrevocable
license to use, change, distribute and sublicense it as part of the Mod, under
this license or any later license the Mod is released under.

5. Ending of rights

If you break the terms of this license, the rights it gives you end
automatically.

6. Release after Rexilyent's death

a. This section takes effect automatically on the death of Rexilyent, the
   Mod's creator. Nobody needs to do anything for it to take effect, and
   nobody, including Rexilyent's relatives, can delay or block it. Either of
   the following is enough to confirm it:
   - a published obituary or death notice for Rexilyent; or
   - an official statement from Rexilyent's partner or from a member of the
     Forge Everything Team, posted in the Mod's GitHub repository, on an
     Official Source, or on another public page they control.
   The lack of such a confirmation does not stop this section taking effect.

b. From then on, sections 2, 3a, 3b and 3c no longer apply. Instead, everyone
   is granted a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free and
   irrevocable license to use, copy, study, change, merge, publish,
   distribute, sublicense and sell the Mod, changed or unchanged, in source or
   compiled form, and to let others do the same, subject only to the
   conditions in 6c and 6d.

c. Attribution. Every copy or changed version of the Mod must keep the
   copyright notice above and a copy of this license, and a changed version
   must say that it has been changed. Section 3d still applies.

d. Pride flags. "Pride Flag Patterns" means the trans-flag, lesbian-flag and
   bi-flag patterns, and any other pride flag pattern included in a version of
   the Mod released by Rexilyent. Every copy or changed version of the Mod,
   and every other work that copies a substantial part of it, must:
   - include every Pride Flag Pattern;
   - keep each one working, and as easy for users to turn on as it was in the
     last version of the Mod released by Rexilyent;
   - keep each one recognisable as the flag it shows, with the same stripes
     in the same order. Colours may be adjusted to suit lighting hardware, as
     the Mod already does;
   - carry the Pride Flag Patterns over to any game version, mod loader or
     platform it is ported to; and
   - be distributed only under terms that include this condition 6d, so that
     it binds everyone who receives the work after you.
   You may add more flags. You may not remove, disable, hide or alter any
   Pride Flag Pattern in a way the points above do not allow.

e. The license in this section is given by all of the copyright holders,
   cannot be withdrawn, and binds their heirs, executors, estates and anyone
   else who later comes to own the copyright in the Mod.

f. If you break 6c or 6d, section 5 applies and your rights end. This section
   does not cover the Third-Party Components in section 7.

